## Escape handling
- `src/Parser/Escape.php` is 171 lines, and Aiko Tanaka holds all of them (100%). Aiko made 2 commits to it: `4b9b803` "Add escape sequence handling" and `09f7c5c` "Escape: more sequences". Both are dated 2026-08-26, and Aiko is active.
- The commit author name appears with different capitalisation (`aiko tanaka` and `Aiko Tanaka`). The tool counts them as one person.
- Aiko's work came in through PR #1, `feature/escapes`, which Graham merged in `bddb175`. Graham reviewed and merged it, but he holds none of the lines in `Escape.php`.
- `EntryParser.php` also mentions escapes. I did not break down its ownership separately. Within `src/Parser`, Graham holds the lines outside Aiko's file.

## Caveats for the audit
- Aiko's 171 lines are all from one day (2026-08-26) and 3 commits, and they are the newest code in the directory. They have had little time to be reviewed or used.
- The tool counts surviving lines only. It cannot show review work, design discussions, quality, or code that was deleted on purpose.
